# Touch & Gesture Support

## Modules

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `shared/lib/touch.ts` | Input type detection (touch/pointer), virtual keyboard, safe-area |
| `shared/lib/gestures.ts` | Swipe, long-press, pinch-to-zoom hooks |
| `styles/index.css` | CSS adaptations for touch (tap targets, hover guard, safe-area, keyboard) |

## Input Mode Detection

```ts
import { useInputMode, isTouchDevice, isCoarsePointer } from "~/shared/lib/touch";

const mode = useInputMode(); // "touch" | "pointer" — reactively switches
```

The module tracks `pointerdown` events — if the last input was `pointerType === "touch"`, the `touch-active` class is set on `<html>`, otherwise `pointer-active`. This works dynamically on hybrid devices (Surface, iPad + mouse).

## Gestures

### Swipe

```tsx
import { useSwipe } from "~/shared/lib/gestures";

const ref = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);

useSwipe(ref, {
  onSwipeLeft: () => navigateForward(),
  onSwipeRight: () => navigateBack(),
  onSwiping: (dx, dy) => { /* animation */ },
  onSwipeEnd: () => { /* reset */ },
}, {
  threshold: 50,      // px minimum distance
  maxDuration: 500,   // ms maximum gesture duration
  edgeOnly: true,     // from screen edge only
  edgeWidth: 30,      // px edge zone
});
```

### Long-press (context menu)

```tsx
import { useLongPress } from "~/shared/lib/gestures";

const ref = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);

useLongPress(ref, (e) => {
  openContextMenu(e.clientX, e.clientY);
}, {
  delay: 500,          // ms before trigger
  moveTolerance: 10,   // px — cancels on movement
});
```

Includes vibration (`navigator.vibrate(30)`) on supported devices.

### Pinch-to-zoom (images)

```tsx
import { usePinch, type PinchState } from "~/shared/lib/gestures";

const ref = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);

usePinch(ref, ({ scale, centerX, centerY }: PinchState) => {
  applyZoom(scale, centerX, centerY);
});
```

## Virtual Keyboard

```tsx
import { useViewportKeyboard } from "~/shared/lib/touch";

function Composer() {
  const { isOpen, keyboardHeight } = useViewportKeyboard();
  // keyboardHeight — keyboard height in px
}
```

CSS variable `--keyboard-height` is updated automatically. Classes:
- `keyboard-aware` — adds padding-bottom equal to keyboard height
- `keyboard-sticky` — fixes element above the keyboard

## CSS Utilities

### Touch targets (WCAG 2.2)

At `@media (pointer: coarse)` all buttons and interactive elements get `min-height: 44px; min-width: 44px`. This is automatic.

### Hover guard

At `@media (hover: none)` Tailwind hover effects are disabled — prevents hover "sticking" after a tap.

### Safe-area insets

```html
<div class="safe-area-bottom">   <!-- padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom) -->
<div class="safe-area-x">        <!-- left + right -->
<div class="safe-area-all">      <!-- all 4 sides -->
```

### Conditional display

```html
<span class="touch-hide">Visible only with mouse</span>
<span class="pointer-hide">Visible only on touch</span>
```

### Scroll

```html
<div class="touch-scroll">  <!-- momentum scrolling on iOS + overscroll contain -->
```

## Rules for AI Agent

### Required

1. **Tap targets >= 44px** — buttons, checkboxes, links, list items. `@media (pointer: coarse)` is already set in CSS, but when creating new components verify sizes
2. **Hover != primary interaction** — hover effects supplement but don't replace tap/click. Information shown on hover must be accessible another way (tooltip → long-press, context menu)
3. **Pointer Events** — use `pointerdown/move/up`, NOT `touchstart/move/end`. Pointer Events unify mouse + touch + pen
4. **passive: true** — all `addEventListener` for touch/pointer should be passive, except cases with `preventDefault`
5. **Safe-area** — on elements adjacent to screen edges (toolbar, composer, navigation), use `safe-area-*` classes

### Forbidden

- **DO NOT** use `touch-action: none` globally — only on specific gesture areas
- **DO NOT** block pinch-to-zoom on document (violates accessibility)
- **DO NOT** rely on double-tap — conflicts with zoom in browsers
- **DO NOT** set `user-scalable=no` in viewport meta

### Context menu

On desktop: right-click (`contextmenu` event).
On touch: long-press via `useLongPress()`.
Both should open the same UI.

### Swipe navigation

Swipe right from left edge → goBack.
Swipe left from right edge → goForward.
Configured in `app/app.tsx` via `useSwipe(rootRef, ..., { edgeOnly: true })`.

### Text fields

`font-size: max(16px, 1em)` is already set globally — prevents auto-zoom on iOS when focusing an input.

### Verification

When implementing touch-dependent features, verify:
1. Chrome DevTools → Toggle device toolbar (Ctrl+Shift+M)
2. Devices with `pointer: coarse` (Touch Simulation enabled)
3. E2E: Playwright with `hasTouch: true` in config
